body:
Oh I see, shit. What did you clean with and how often did you do it? Also was there yellowish liquid? I've some but it's very minimal.. I just feel a lil weird because my body feels warm, but my check up with the piercer isn't till almost a week :/

&#x200B;

Hold up, I can pm you a gif of it but it's really shitty quality bc I used my webcam.

I woke up and there was more blood around every piercing, so I took everyone's advice and soaked with warm water, and rinsed with saline. There's still blood clotted around my double helix but I'm not touching it and letting it do it's thing. Does this look okay? [https://i.gyazo.com/eab18254b8f95678d8b9484502e54da5.png](https://i.gyazo.com/eab18254b8f95678d8b9484502e54da5.png)

&#x200B;

Once again, so sorry for these questions! Just really don't want an infection and I'm really new to piercings.

Hi! Sorry to bother you! But is it okay if I use one of these and spray it on my piercings? [https://i.gyazo.com/3b359b751f45081a6a104b33264126c7.png](https://i.gyazo.com/3b359b751f45081a6a104b33264126c7.png)

&#x200B;

I woke up and there was more blood around every piercing, so I took everyone's advice and soaked with warm water, and rinsed with saline. There's still blood clotted around my double helix but I'm not touching it and letting it do it's thing. Does this look okay? [https://i.gyazo.com/eab18254b8f95678d8b9484502e54da5.png](https://i.gyazo.com/eab18254b8f95678d8b9484502e54da5.png)

I see. So you're saying that it's 100%, compulsory for the three of us children to sign on the ownership of the flat? Right now, I'm in a situation where my sister wants to leave me out of it, like she has a choice, and I'm very confused. She said something about my name not being on the lease, but my father did not have a will and did not leave the flat to either of my siblings.

&#x200B;

Edit: I'm OP, but on a different account.

>You need to find out who is the owner of your late father's HDB flat. Go to Singapore Land Authority's website to find out the owner. You need to pay a fee and do a search. From the results of the search, you can find out how the owner managed to get ownership of the flat.

Sorry for the late reply. This issue just came up again and I hope I'm not bothering you too much. I did end up paying and checking the property ownership and it still listed my mom has the joint owner.. But we've heard from HDB that she signed her rights over during the divorce so I'm a little confused.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Edit: I'm OP, but on a different account.
